  {'title':'Bruß, distributed dense-coding contribution, Oberwolfach Report 4/2005','url':'https://ems.press/content/serial-article-files/45978','note':'Printed pages 203–205 explicitly ask whether the four-qubit W state belongs to the LOCC-dense-codeable class.'},
  {'title':'Winter, The capacity of the quantum multiple-access channel','url':'https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/9807019v3','note':'Theorem 9 gives product-prior multiple-access achievability with separate encoder maps and vanishing uniform average error. Its single quantum output must be available in one receiver’s laboratory.'},
  {'title':'Pradhan, Agrawal and Pati, Teleportation and superdense coding with genuine quadripartite entangled states','url':'https://arxiv.org/abs/0705.1917v1','note':'Section 4.2.3 already uses Bell measurements and classical forwarding for a two-bit W-state protocol. The present protocol retains the second receiver’s quantum output for many-copy decoding.'},
  {'title':'Cao and Song, Quantum secure direct communication with W state','url':'https://doi.org/10.1088/0256-307X/23/2/005','note':'An earlier W-state communication scheme using Bell measurements and classical communication, credited by the manuscript for its paired Bell decomposition. Its security task is distinct from the independent-message rate theorem here.'},
  {'title':'Huang, Zhang and Hou, Classical capacity of a quantum multiple-access channel','url':'https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/9911120v5','note':'Earlier work already connects multiple-access coding with dense coding. That general connection is not claimed as a new idea here.'},
  {'title':'Hayashi and Wang, Dense Coding with Locality Restriction on Decoders','url':'https://doi.org/10.1103/PRXQuantum.3.030346','note':'Studies a sender, receiver and helper with a different ownership and transmission arrangement. Its capacity formula cannot be imported without checking the receiver partition used here.'}
